{"title":"Computer science books","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>These <b>Computer Science books</b> are recommended by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Art_of_Problem_Solving\" title=\"Art of Problem Solving\">Art of Problem Solving</a> administrators and members of the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community\">AoPS Community</a>.\n</p><p>Before adding any books to this page, please review the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AoPS_Wiki:Linking_books\" title=\"AoPS Wiki:Linking books\">AoPS Wiki:Linking books</a> page.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Books_by_subject\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Books by subject</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Artificial_Intelligence\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Artificial Intelligence</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Digital_Logic\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Digital Logic</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Information_Theory\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Information Theory</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Programming_and_Algorithms\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Programming and Algorithms</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Books_by_Knuth\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Books by Knuth</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Competition_Problems\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Competition Problems</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Books_by_subject\">Books by subject</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Computer_science_books&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Books by subject\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Artificial_Intelligence\">Artificial Intelligence</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Computer_science_books&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Artificial Intelligence\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0262581116/artofproblems-20\">Adaptation in Natural and Artificial Systems</a> by John H. Holland.</li></ul>\n<p><br />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Digital_Logic\">Digital Logic</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Computer_science_books&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Digital Logic\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0780334264/artofproblems-20\">Ones and Zeros: Understanding Boolean Algebra, Digital Circuits and the Logic of Sets</a> by John Gregg.</li></ul>\n<p><br />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Information_Theory\">Information Theory</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Computer_science_books&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Information Theory\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0486240614/artofproblems-20\">An Introduction to Information Theory</a> by J.R. Pierce.</li></ul>\n<p><br />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Programming_and_Algorithms\">Programming and Algorithms</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Computer_science_books&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Programming and Algorithms\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//mitpressbookstore.mit.edu/book/9780262543231\">Structure and Interpretation of Computer Programs</a> by Hal Abelson Jerry Sussman and Julie Sussman.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0262032937/artofproblems-20\">Introduction to Algorithms</a> by Thomas H. Cormen, Charles E. Leiserson, Ronald L. Rivest and Clifford Stein.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/3030542556/artofproblems-20\">The Algorithm Design Manual</a> by Steven S. Skiena.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Books_by_Knuth\">Books by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=D._E._Knuth&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"D. E. Knuth (page does not exist)\">Knuth</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Computer_science_books&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Books by Knuth\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0201485419/artofproblems-20\">The Art of Computer Programming Volumes 1-3 (boxed set)</a> by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=D._E._Knuth&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"D. E. Knuth (page does not exist)\">D. E. Knuth</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Competition_Problems\">Competition Problems</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Computer_science_books&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Competition Problems\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//shop.amt.edu.au/products/aic1\">Australia Informatics Competition Problems 2005-2010</a></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Computer_science_books&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Computer_science\" title=\"Computer science\">Computer science</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.beestar.org/exercise/ref_list_smcs.jsp?&amp;mid=1500&amp;div=9\">Computer Science Reading for Grade 3-5, 6-8</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Informatics\" title=\"Informatics\">Informatics</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Informatics_competitions\" title=\"Informatics competitions\">Informatics competitions</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Science\" title=\"Science\">Science</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://olympiads.win.tue.nl/ioi/study/books.html\">Reading List</a> (someone have a linky?)</li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017235430\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.015 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.026 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 30/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 31/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:1479:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017235430 and revision id 282699. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}